WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.276 --> 00:00:07.333
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:13.778
Hm. This is actually a little more
degrading than a dunking booth,

00:00:13.778 --> 00:00:17.658
because in a dunking booth, someone
else has to actively dunk you,

00:00:17.658 --> 00:00:20.125
but here I'm expected to dunk myself.

00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:21.860
Is this really the way, though?

00:00:22.483 --> 00:00:24.381
Okay, that way's on fire...

00:00:25.521 --> 00:00:28.756
Yeah, he hung the bodies out
for me--this has to be it.

00:00:28.756 --> 00:00:30.791
And I could probably
find another way around,

00:00:30.791 --> 00:00:33.196
but I admit, this does look fun.

00:00:33.196 --> 00:00:35.216
Yeah, fun's been out of stock lately.

00:00:35.216 --> 00:00:38.757
Everybody who had fun is dead,
which depletes even more fun.

00:00:38.757 --> 00:00:40.412
All right, enough stalling. Let's go.

00:00:40.412 --> 00:00:41.923
HOOOOOOO!

00:00:41.923 --> 00:00:43.439
[underwater HOOOOO!]

00:00:44.409 --> 00:00:48.795
That was pretty good! I'm going to have
to ask him for the video footage to that.

00:00:48.795 --> 00:00:53.163
I wanted to do a flip, but I wasn't
100% sure I wouldn't hit the rim.

00:00:53.163 --> 00:00:56.562
This isn't basketball; I lose
all my points if I hit the rim,

00:00:56.562 --> 00:00:58.076
especially with my head.

00:00:58.076 --> 00:01:00.865
Yeah, if there are extra nooses
there, and I somehow hit one,

00:01:00.865 --> 00:01:02.967
that'd probably take my head clean off, huh?

00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:07.696
And if we're being real, that's probably
the coolest way possible to go, but not me!

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.438
Shit!

00:01:10.504 --> 00:01:11.004
What...?

00:01:14.571 --> 00:01:15.981
Yeah! Over there!

00:01:15.981 --> 00:01:19.164
I need to reload! Just calm down already!

00:01:19.164 --> 00:01:21.022
He must be giving them sugar water.

00:01:21.621 --> 00:01:22.807
OH MY GOD!

00:01:22.807 --> 00:01:24.427
[fast zombie screaming]
OUTSIDE!

00:01:25.238 --> 00:01:27.274
You're worse than salesmen!

00:01:27.274 --> 00:01:31.534
I remember when salesmen were kind of dying
off, though. It was probably dangerous.

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:35.980
I wonder if someone ever blew one away
with a shotgun. It had to have happened.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.201
Yeah, stay on your side.

00:01:38.201 --> 00:01:39.004
[glass shattering]

00:01:39.004 --> 00:01:40.940
ARE YOU FUCKING KIDDING ME?!

00:01:41.951 --> 00:01:42.736
AHH!

00:01:42.736 --> 00:01:45.445
YOU HAVE THE ENTIRE OUTDOORS TO PLAY IN!

00:01:45.843 --> 00:01:48.874
BUT NO! YOU HAVE TO CHOOSE THIS ONE ROOM!

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:51.558
This room sucks, anyway! You can have it!

00:01:51.558 --> 00:01:53.946
It won't even keep the rain out, now.

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:57.286
You can have fun attacking
the trash or something.

00:01:57.286 --> 00:01:58.468
Or eat it, maybe.

00:01:59.194 --> 00:02:01.562
Yeah, this IS going to be a long night.

00:02:02.209 --> 00:02:02.955
[clanging]

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.031
Whoa! Just tuning the elevator.

00:02:05.031 --> 00:02:05.644
[clanging]

00:02:05.644 --> 00:02:06.535
Pling!

00:02:08.057 --> 00:02:08.728
Nope!

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.778
You are NOT Santa Claus.

00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.400
Yeah, this is worse than
my old neighborhood, too.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.557
This is more like Harry's neighborhood.

00:02:16.557 --> 00:02:19.486
Harry's neighborhood was this
bad--especially at night.

00:02:19.486 --> 00:02:20.964
They would climb the walls there.

00:02:21.718 --> 00:02:23.883
Yeah, his dad fired
a shotgun at the ceiling,

00:02:23.883 --> 00:02:25.480
and he only scared SOME of them off.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:26.548
[glass shattering]
Whoop!

00:02:27.732 --> 00:02:29.318
Oh shit, are those drugs?!

00:02:29.318 --> 00:02:32.220
No, it's just rubbing alcohol. I knew that.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.547
I'm losing my edge.

00:02:33.547 --> 00:02:35.996
Yeah, Harry was in a BAD neighborhood.

00:02:35.996 --> 00:02:37.699
He said the cops stopped coming there.

00:02:37.699 --> 00:02:40.425
Yeah, his dad had to go to court, didn't he?

00:02:40.425 --> 00:02:42.083
Because he set a bear trap
in the fireplace, and--

00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:42.675
[fast zombie screams]

00:02:42.675 --> 00:02:43.756
Whoa! What the fuck?

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:49.067
But yeah, he set a bear trap, so when the
burglars or whoever came down the chimney

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:49.914
it would get them,

00:02:49.914 --> 00:02:53.378
except one came down headfirst
and it took his head clean off.

00:02:53.378 --> 00:02:56.705
I remember his mom got pissed because
it got blood all over the carpet.

00:02:56.705 --> 00:02:57.971
[deep groaning]

00:02:57.971 --> 00:02:58.700
What the hell?

00:03:00.454 --> 00:03:02.272
Your name is Lumpy.

00:03:02.272 --> 00:03:02.974
WHOA!

00:03:03.292 --> 00:03:04.589
How is it standing?!

00:03:05.493 --> 00:03:06.095
CHRIST!

00:03:07.139 --> 00:03:10.717
Oh, that's great. Spread everywhere
and they're still not dead.

00:03:10.717 --> 00:03:11.877
Is this birdshot?

00:03:12.669 --> 00:03:13.190
God...

00:03:13.666 --> 00:03:14.200
BLUH!

00:03:15.248 --> 00:03:16.512
This is horrible...

00:03:17.511 --> 00:03:18.891
...but I should be happy...

00:03:19.858 --> 00:03:21.170
...that they're this big.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:24.788
What if these things were the size of
ticks, but still took my brain over?

00:03:24.788 --> 00:03:26.435
That would more horrible.

00:03:26.435 --> 00:03:29.499
Shit, it's only been a day
or two since I first got bit.

00:03:29.499 --> 00:03:31.281
I might be infected anyway.

00:03:31.281 --> 00:03:34.268
I was breathing those god
damn spores yesterday!

00:03:34.268 --> 00:03:36.939
Oh my God, is it still alive?

00:03:37.972 --> 00:03:40.007
No. It's not.

00:03:40.007 --> 00:03:43.318
Okay, it wasn't LITERALLY yesterday, but...

00:03:44.383 --> 00:03:48.185
biologically it was. I think.

00:03:48.185 --> 00:03:49.431
I don't know...

00:03:49.431 --> 00:03:53.432
It might have been a few days, because
I felt pretty good this morning.

00:03:53.432 --> 00:03:54.262
Physically.

00:03:54.262 --> 00:03:56.808
Mentally, the nightmare
never really stopped.

00:03:56.808 --> 00:04:00.128
[low howling]

00:04:00.128 --> 00:04:02.236
Somebody needs to feed their dog.

00:04:02.236 --> 00:04:04.139
But, yeah, the last that--Oh!

00:04:06.476 --> 00:04:08.081
Soccer evolved.

00:04:09.588 --> 00:04:11.802
Shit. Blood all over the wall.

00:04:11.802 --> 00:04:13.336
He must have offed himself.

00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:16.327
And there's the weapon.
I could've been a detective.

00:04:16.327 --> 00:04:18.615
Although I haven't solved my own case.

00:04:18.615 --> 00:04:22.114
The last thing I remember before
waking up was that space train,

00:04:22.114 --> 00:04:24.004
and I felt like shit then.

00:04:24.004 --> 00:04:25.846
Absolute shit.

00:04:26.969 --> 00:04:28.063
You missed!

00:04:29.878 --> 00:04:31.107
Still missed!

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:33.293
Oh.

00:04:33.293 --> 00:04:34.362
Great.

00:04:34.362 --> 00:04:37.056
But, yeah, I don't even
remember falling asleep.

00:04:37.056 --> 00:04:39.180
He must have shot me up with something.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:44.294
But the question: Is there an alien
infection still growing inside of me?

00:04:44.294 --> 00:04:47.801
I don't feel different, but maybe it
wouldn't want me to feel different.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:49.402
[fast zombies yowling]

00:04:49.402 --> 00:04:51.979
Dammit... Flying dogs...

00:04:51.979 --> 00:04:56.250
Well, I haven't seen anyone obviously
infected with an alien virus.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.556
[rumbling sound]
I have seen a lot of dead people, though.

00:04:58.556 --> 00:04:59.309
What was that?

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:01.184
Oh HELL no!

00:05:02.406 --> 00:05:03.131
Uh uh!

00:05:03.548 --> 00:05:06.349
The Hunchback of God Damn.

00:05:07.798 --> 00:05:10.418
This is no fucking good.

00:05:10.932 --> 00:05:12.199
That's a little better.

00:05:12.199 --> 00:05:14.517
And you know what? I'm not
even going to look to see if

00:05:14.517 --> 00:05:17.964
even smaller huggers start spilling
out of the one I just shot.

00:05:17.964 --> 00:05:19.165
I don't need to know that.

00:05:19.165 --> 00:05:21.799
That goes DOUBLE since I'm unemployed.

00:05:21.799 --> 00:05:26.172
No, wait! I forgot! I'm working for the
government that doesn't exist anymore!

00:05:26.856 --> 00:05:27.561
Yeah.

00:05:28.773 --> 00:05:30.909
I'm working at a job that doesn't pay me,

00:05:30.909 --> 00:05:35.339
has no description or objectives, and a
boss that runs away every time he sees me.

00:05:35.339 --> 00:05:39.176
Which would be great, except for
the payment part. I'm a vagrant.

00:05:40.013 --> 00:05:42.893
To be fair, maybe money doesn't exist now.

00:05:42.893 --> 00:05:44.528
But barter does.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:49.406
What the...? Where'd you come from?
Did you climb the fence, or...?

00:05:49.925 --> 00:05:50.851
It doesn't matter.

00:05:51.448 --> 00:05:54.942
But yeah, he could've given
me food, a place to live,

00:05:54.942 --> 00:05:57.321
police protection--that'd be a good one.

00:05:57.321 --> 00:06:00.970
But yeah, why pay someone when you can
just watch them run around in fear.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.355
Doesn't sound like a stable economic system.

00:06:03.355 --> 00:06:07.317
What? Now where did YOU come
from? Are you following me?

00:06:07.844 --> 00:06:08.722
Who sent you?

00:06:09.325 --> 00:06:11.806
Did we do that thing where you
look for someone in a store,

00:06:11.806 --> 00:06:15.770
but you each look in the wrong aisle at the
same time so you think they're not there?

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.265
What...? Where are they coming from?

00:06:18.265 --> 00:06:20.994
No. I don't have the ammo
to do this all night.

00:06:20.994 --> 00:06:23.211
I've already used more than I wanted to.

00:06:23.211 --> 00:06:27.406
That is the one upside to shooting
cops: they have bullets on them.

00:06:27.406 --> 00:06:30.036
You guys are a dead end
in the bullet economy.

00:06:30.036 --> 00:06:31.814
I'm not running a charity here.

00:06:31.814 --> 00:06:35.434
Maybe Greg has a trap door that
releases zombies when I'm not looking.

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:38.010
Oh, that's a lever!
He DOES have a trap door!

00:06:39.563 --> 00:06:40.082
Oh.

00:06:41.815 --> 00:06:42.446
Huh.

00:06:44.711 --> 00:06:46.244
Well that did a lot.

00:06:46.971 --> 00:06:48.562
Yeah, there he is.

00:06:48.562 --> 00:06:50.367
Wait, no, there's more behind him.

00:06:51.072 --> 00:06:52.877
Holy shit, how many are there?

00:06:52.877 --> 00:06:55.574
I was wondering why he would
leave this out in the open.

00:06:55.574 --> 00:06:57.866
That's actually genius showmanship--

00:06:57.866 --> 00:07:00.726
tricking the contestants
into trapping themselves.

00:07:00.726 --> 00:07:02.446
All right, let's do this.

00:07:03.297 --> 00:07:06.329
Wait, where did your friends
go? They got lost all ready?

00:07:06.329 --> 00:07:08.872
Eh, this is what I get
for trying to be clever.

00:07:08.872 --> 00:07:10.065
You outdumb me.

00:07:10.861 --> 00:07:13.064
And I'm just assuming these are zombies.

00:07:13.064 --> 00:07:16.616
It's possible he hired actors as
extras and I'm blowing them away.

00:07:16.616 --> 00:07:20.133
Oh, there we go. All right. Another test.

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:24.827
Step number one: Remove
explosive. That's the first test.

00:07:24.827 --> 00:07:28.468
Step number two: Don't
literally cut my own head off.

00:07:28.468 --> 00:07:32.199
That would make a better show, but
he can find someone else for that.

00:07:32.199 --> 00:07:33.024
Step number thr--

00:07:34.783 --> 00:07:37.449
I didn't fail the test. The test failed me.

00:07:37.449 --> 00:07:39.629
Yeah, that's the part they
leave out of MacGyver,

00:07:39.629 --> 00:07:43.722
how all this cobbled-together engineering
tends to fall apart in a few minutes.

00:07:43.722 --> 00:07:46.420
I still can't get over how quiet this is.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:51.005
Hey, I haven't seen the spook for a while
either. That can't be a coincidence.

00:07:51.005 --> 00:07:53.301
I think I'm going to have to kill him.

00:07:53.301 --> 00:07:54.363
[lock jiggles]
No...

00:07:54.363 --> 00:07:57.461
But I have to think this through;
I can't come at him half-cocked,

00:07:57.461 --> 00:07:58.267
because--

00:07:58.267 --> 00:07:59.524
This is what I mean.

00:07:59.524 --> 00:08:00.648
Yeah, you're helping.

00:08:00.994 --> 00:08:01.557
Whoa!

00:08:01.557 --> 00:08:02.361
No, you're not.

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:04.466
But you do support my theory.

00:08:04.466 --> 00:08:07.400
Fuck this. You guys can
hug it out. I'm leaving.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:09.156
Why can't they attack each other?

00:08:09.156 --> 00:08:10.456
[fast zombie screaming]
HEY!

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:11.449
[fast zombie screaming]
AH!

00:08:11.449 --> 00:08:12.864
Where are they coming from?!

00:08:13.717 --> 00:08:14.921
Oh-ho!

00:08:15.757 --> 00:08:16.563
AH!

00:08:16.563 --> 00:08:20.316
MOST ANIMALS ARE SCARED OF
GUNSHOTS! WHAT THE FUCK?!

00:08:20.316 --> 00:08:23.244
Yeah, this is a LOT
like Harry's neighborhood.

00:08:23.244 --> 00:08:26.234
It's just that nobody's armed and--
Wait, WHAT?

00:08:26.234 --> 00:08:28.322
Are they parachuting in?!

00:08:29.728 --> 00:08:30.565
BLAH!

00:08:30.565 --> 00:08:33.704
Hey, I'm kind of getting low on shells!

00:08:33.704 --> 00:08:35.028
I don't want to be that guy that says,

00:08:35.028 --> 00:08:39.958
"Gee, I wish I could blow away someone
with a shotgun," then click, nothing.

00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:41.374
You know what I'm saying?

00:08:41.374 --> 00:08:42.856
Okay, one more shot.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:46.659
Dammit, these aren't dependable.

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:50.860
See, we're overcomplicating this.
Just simplify my life, please.

00:08:51.792 --> 00:08:53.655
Well, I can still count on SOMEBODY.

00:08:55.894 --> 00:08:57.707
I don't know how much ammo I have.

00:09:00.357 --> 00:09:03.596
I said I wasn't going to burn
through my ammo, and now look at me.

00:09:03.596 --> 00:09:04.577
I'm ashamed.

00:09:04.577 --> 00:09:06.045
No, YOU should be ashamed.

00:09:06.847 --> 00:09:08.377
THERE WE GO AGAIN!

00:09:09.054 --> 00:09:09.659
FUCK!

00:09:11.203 --> 00:09:14.505
[gun clicks]
Oh no. Today is NOT Loose End Day.

00:09:14.505 --> 00:09:16.640
Check your calendar; you'll see I'm right!

00:09:18.236 --> 00:09:19.557
Wasn't there enough--Yes?

00:09:21.077 --> 00:09:23.625
What? You win. You can have that spot.

00:09:24.693 --> 00:09:25.751
Yeah, I should've clarified--

00:09:25.751 --> 00:09:27.692
[gun clicks]
Oh hell, I'm out.

00:09:27.692 --> 00:09:28.718
FINE!

00:09:28.718 --> 00:09:29.649
One shell!

00:09:29.931 --> 00:09:30.890
Two shells!

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.437
Wah! Three shells!

00:09:33.389 --> 00:09:36.267
Foooooouuuuuur shells!

00:09:36.267 --> 00:09:38.812
TWO! I HAVE TWO SHELLS LEFT!

00:09:38.812 --> 00:09:42.332
This message was brought to you
by Broken Economy Sesame Street.

00:09:42.332 --> 00:09:46.600
Yeah, I meant to say it's not Loose
End Day for vicious scurrying things.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.736
I can't afford to apply it to everyone.

00:09:48.736 --> 00:09:49.275
OHH!

00:09:50.525 --> 00:09:53.572
You should never let your
ambitions exceed your ammo supply.

00:09:53.572 --> 00:09:54.884
Hey, there's nothing here.

00:09:55.784 --> 00:09:59.339
Besides, the small ones
CAN go down in one shot.

00:09:59.339 --> 00:10:03.021
That was the problem with the
hunchback--he was like a moose.

00:10:03.021 --> 00:10:03.653
Mm-mm.

00:10:06.926 --> 00:10:09.796
And that is the lesson to be learned here.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:16.699
If I shoot the spook in the face point
blank, I cannot assume that will kill him.

00:10:16.699 --> 00:10:18.536
He has advanced technology.

00:10:18.996 --> 00:10:20.846
I have to be smart about this.

00:10:20.846 --> 00:10:22.498
I mean he's not stupid,

00:10:22.498 --> 00:10:23.586
he has to assume that I...

00:10:23.586 --> 00:10:24.276
[poison headcrab chirps]

00:10:25.656 --> 00:10:27.222
Oh, get fucked!

00:10:27.737 --> 00:10:31.240
It was following me on the
ledge like a mountain goat!

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:32.902
Oh, now what is this?!

00:10:32.902 --> 00:10:36.098
Yeah, yeah. Nice try. Real stable.

00:10:36.098 --> 00:10:38.007
Stupid game show.

00:10:38.293 --> 00:10:40.543
I'm sure he has cameras set up here.

00:10:40.543 --> 00:10:41.689
I hope he doesn't do that thing

00:10:41.689 --> 00:10:46.836
where you saw the board halfway from the
underside so it looks stable, then crack.

00:10:46.836 --> 00:10:48.586
Oh, his vacation spot.

00:10:48.586 --> 00:10:50.361
Why does he have two shotguns?

00:10:50.361 --> 00:10:51.408
Grenades...

00:10:51.408 --> 00:10:53.277
Of course, the beer's empty.

00:10:53.277 --> 00:10:55.797
Hey, one of these grenades fits in my gun.

00:10:55.797 --> 00:10:56.709
[low yowling]
What was that?

00:10:57.883 --> 00:10:58.890
WHOA!

00:10:59.549 --> 00:11:02.130
Is this an event? Am I the judge?

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:03.720
Was I supposed to judge that?

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:07.413
Well, you missed me, and the
roof, so I give that a 10.

00:11:07.413 --> 00:11:09.892
Though I don't usually
operate on a number scale.

00:11:09.892 --> 00:11:12.837
It's a hit-me-and-I-shoot-you-in-the-face scale.

00:11:12.837 --> 00:11:14.526
There's not much of a spectrum there.

00:11:14.997 --> 00:11:17.140
Okay, I'm NOT going in a circle.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:19.721
I'm going in a spiral. I gained height.

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:23.999
Another shotgun. Ammo box.
Yeah! I can use it.

00:11:23.999 --> 00:11:25.351
Like...right now.

00:11:26.041 --> 00:11:29.925
Yeah, I'm thinking Greg might be like
Eddie, where he keeps like ten guns

00:11:29.925 --> 00:11:32.909
spread around different rooms
in his house for quick access.

00:11:32.909 --> 00:11:35.904
It doesn't explain two shotguns
in the same place, though.

00:11:35.904 --> 00:11:36.647
What?

00:11:36.647 --> 00:11:39.380
[screaming]

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:43.421
NEVER FORGET! THERE'S ALWAYS
SOMEONE BEHIND ME! LIKE HIM!

00:11:43.421 --> 00:11:44.327
[exhales]

00:11:44.327 --> 00:11:46.987
Okay, so we know he likes
Schwarzenegger movies.

00:11:46.987 --> 00:11:51.466
Maybe he saw "Terminator 2" and was like,
"I can fire a shotgun with one hand."

00:11:51.466 --> 00:11:53.756
Tried it once with two of them, then quit.

00:11:53.756 --> 00:11:54.826
I should just ask him.

00:11:56.444 --> 00:11:58.448
[screaming]
[fast zombies screaming]

00:11:58.448 --> 00:11:59.491
AAAHHHH!

00:11:59.491 --> 00:12:01.607
MY LEG!
GRIGORI: The grave holds nothing less for you.

00:12:02.317 --> 00:12:05.778
FUCK! This is NOT--AHH!

00:12:05.778 --> 00:12:07.345
GET OFF MY ASS!

00:12:09.642 --> 00:12:10.262
FUCK!

00:12:11.237 --> 00:12:12.737
Agh, that hurts!

00:12:12.737 --> 00:12:15.827
I can't believe I fell
off the fucking building!

00:12:15.827 --> 00:12:18.410
There is no crowdsurfing in hell.

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:19.922
Jeez, that's sore.

00:12:19.922 --> 00:12:23.189
I didn't even hit the dirt. It
was right on the cobblestone.

00:12:23.189 --> 00:12:24.696
[fast zombies chittering]
Okay, am I good?

00:12:24.696 --> 00:12:25.438
What's that sound?

00:12:26.602 --> 00:12:29.159
Jesus! Zombie Jordan!

00:12:29.159 --> 00:12:31.119
BACK OFF! I DON'T HAVE THE BALL!

00:12:31.119 --> 00:12:32.482
I DON'T HAVE THE BALL!

00:12:32.482 --> 00:12:33.149
FUCK YOU!

00:12:33.593 --> 00:12:34.602
[gun clicking]
CRAP!

00:12:37.241 --> 00:12:37.741
Hup!

00:12:39.779 --> 00:12:40.630
Step off!

00:12:41.761 --> 00:12:44.192
This is bullshit! What's with these teams?!

00:12:45.215 --> 00:12:45.715
Fuck...

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:47.363
There you...

00:12:48.154 --> 00:12:49.824
[poison headcrab squeals]
HOOO!

00:12:50.079 --> 00:12:50.797
No!

00:12:51.514 --> 00:12:52.673
What are YOU looking at?!

00:12:53.434 --> 00:12:57.618
Oh, perfect! I've got
FIVE shells left. FIVE!

00:12:57.618 --> 00:12:58.781
Can you believe it?

00:12:58.781 --> 00:13:00.032
Don't answer that.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.182
Okay, FOUR!

00:13:02.182 --> 00:13:04.614
I've gotta change my lifestyle here.

00:13:04.614 --> 00:13:06.147
Okay, I picked up a magazine.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:10.029
What's going on?!

00:13:10.029 --> 00:13:11.987
Does he have a plate in his head?

00:13:11.987 --> 00:13:14.481
[poison headcrab zombie yowls]
Okay, I guess this is a better caliber.

00:13:14.481 --> 00:13:18.858
Well, I guess this is what Harry was going
through, short of falling off a building.

00:13:20.051 --> 00:13:21.413
And the zombies.

00:13:21.413 --> 00:13:24.013
After dark, this may as
well be his neighborhood.

00:13:25.122 --> 00:13:28.011
Yeah, didn't he say there was
a movie his life was like?

00:13:28.011 --> 00:13:29.601
A John Carpenter one?

00:13:29.601 --> 00:13:34.148
Attack on Police... Assault on
Precinct... Something like that.

00:13:34.148 --> 00:13:36.930
I wonder if that Greg guy knows
which one I'm talking about.

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:39.622
Yeah, THIS board. I didn't forget THAT.

00:13:40.511 --> 00:13:42.591
I don't need to fall TWICE tonight.

00:13:42.591 --> 00:13:44.057
I'm sure Greg's going to be watching

00:13:44.057 --> 00:13:47.119
the first time in slow
motion before he goes to bed.

00:13:47.119 --> 00:13:50.565
Some people dream about falling.
He'll be dreaming about ME falling.

00:13:52.307 --> 00:13:55.993
I bet the spook knows which movie I'm
talking about, though he'll never tell me.

00:13:55.993 --> 00:13:58.012
I mean, he probably
doesn't know off the cuff.

00:13:58.693 --> 00:14:00.148
But he strikes me as the sort of guy

00:14:00.148 --> 00:14:02.983
who has access to all knowledge
in the known universe.

00:14:02.983 --> 00:14:03.905
He gives me that vibe.

00:14:03.905 --> 00:14:06.246
GRIGORI: I remember your TRUE face.

00:14:06.246 --> 00:14:07.415
Oh boy.

00:14:08.413 --> 00:14:09.448
Well...

00:14:09.448 --> 00:14:12.951
That DOES sound like something
a rooftop shooter would say,

00:14:12.951 --> 00:14:14.837
even before the invasion.

00:14:14.837 --> 00:14:15.985
What's he looking at?

00:14:15.985 --> 00:14:17.449
I wonder if he does mushrooms.

00:14:17.449 --> 00:14:22.065
GRIGORI: How came you here, brother?
This is the wrong side of town for you.

00:14:22.065 --> 00:14:24.603
GRIGORI: Did I not tell
you to seek the church?

00:14:24.603 --> 00:14:27.337
GRIGORI: Mend your ways
before it is too late.

00:14:27.337 --> 00:14:28.250
Uh huh.

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:31.114
You know, life is obviously
harder if you're crazy,

00:14:31.114 --> 00:14:33.039
but then do you KNOW it's harder?

00:14:33.039 --> 00:14:35.803
Dammit, I forgot to ask him
about John Carpenter movies.

00:14:36.503 --> 00:14:38.932
[screaming]

00:14:38.932 --> 00:14:40.352
OWW!

00:14:40.352 --> 00:14:42.152
Did he rig this to fall?!

00:14:42.152 --> 00:14:43.139
[growling]

00:14:43.139 --> 00:14:46.003
Hey, isn't that a child psychology thing?

00:14:46.003 --> 00:14:49.878
He knows where the church is, so he
assumes *I* know where the church is?

00:14:49.878 --> 00:14:51.686
Life must be confusing for him.

00:14:55.199 --> 00:14:58.038
[shotgun clicks]
Oh shit! I'm spent! I forgot!

00:14:58.711 --> 00:14:59.570
That's...

00:14:59.570 --> 00:15:00.318
...what...

00:15:00.318 --> 00:15:01.037
...the...

00:15:01.037 --> 00:15:02.548
...sidearms...

00:15:02.548 --> 00:15:03.570
...are for.

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:04.771
BLAH!

00:15:04.771 --> 00:15:05.554
Shit!

00:15:06.154 --> 00:15:07.450
NGAH!

00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:10.796
Y'know, chicks dig scars,
but I think there's a limit.

00:15:10.796 --> 00:15:12.515
It's probably a bell curve.

00:15:12.515 --> 00:15:16.354
If people start calling me "Blenderface",
this is going to work against me.

00:15:16.354 --> 00:15:18.290
No. We're not doing this.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:21.067
If I give you a bullet now,
you're just going to want more.

00:15:21.947 --> 00:15:24.885
Okay, fine. One more. One.

00:15:25.995 --> 00:15:30.219
Hm. Maybe he had two shotguns so if
he ran out of ammo in the first one,

00:15:30.219 --> 00:15:31.915
he wouldn't have to reload.

00:15:31.915 --> 00:15:33.940
But he was already carrying a shotgun.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:35.805
He needed three shotguns?

00:15:36.374 --> 00:15:37.483
Yeah, wonderful.

00:15:37.483 --> 00:15:39.979
These are my last six Magnum rounds.

00:15:39.979 --> 00:15:41.143
[glass shattering]
It b--

00:15:41.143 --> 00:15:42.519
What was that?

00:15:42.519 --> 00:15:44.200
I wonder if it's the spook.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.690
He WAS following me.

00:15:45.690 --> 00:15:47.862
I hope I lost him, but, y'know...

00:15:49.458 --> 00:15:51.183
Yeah, I might need to kill him.

00:15:51.183 --> 00:15:52.367
I shouldn't shoot him.

00:15:52.367 --> 00:15:55.080
What I should try is throwing
stuff at him casually,

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.846
like I'm playfully annoyed with him,

00:15:56.846 --> 00:15:58.818
like a stick, a can,

00:15:58.818 --> 00:16:03.283
then just slip in a jagged chunk of metal
coated in poison. See how that goes.

00:16:03.283 --> 00:16:05.033
Wait a minute! I've been here!

00:16:05.033 --> 00:16:08.888
Oh, for GOD'S SAKE! I *AM* going in circles!

00:16:08.888 --> 00:16:12.250
Great! Now I'm thinking
like a Blenderface...

00:16:15.489 --> 00:16:19.348
Y'know, it wouldn't be such a loss
if they DID start bombing here.

